---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import ProjectTags from "../../components/ProjectTags.astro";
import HexapodArchitecture from "../../components/HexapodArchitecture.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout>
  <article class="hexapod space-y-12">
    <header id="overview">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-5">Hexapod: Spider</h1>
      <div class="overview-images">
        <figure>
          <img src="/media/hexapod/silva.png" alt="Earlier SILVA hexapod with exposed chassis and six articulated legs" width="1104" height="894" />
          <figcaption>SILVA: earlier platform</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <img src="/media/hexapod/spider.png" alt="Spider hexapod with a black 3D-printed body and leg structure" width="1240" height="922" />
          <figcaption>Spider: updated platform</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <ul class="points">
        <li>Spider builds on the earlier SILVA platform, with a 3D-printed body and leg structure.</li>
        <li>18-actuator platform at UCLA’s Robotics and Mechanisms Laboratory (RoMeLa), being prepared for an art museum installation in Korea.</li>
        <li>My work: coordinated joint trajectories, Python motor-control software, an operator dashboard, and ROS 2 diagnostics.</li>
      </ul>
      <ProjectTags />
    </header>

    <figure id="art-motion">
      <video autoplay loop controls muted playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/media/hexapod/spider-art-poster.jpg" class="w-full aspect-[4/3] object-contain">
        <source src="/media/hexapod/spider-art.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <figcaption>Coordinated art motion on the supported robot.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section id="installation" class="space-y-4">
      <h2>Installation Concept</h2>
      <figure class="concept">
        <img src="/media/hexapod/spider-concept.png" alt="Installation concept with the suspended hexapod casting two shadows onto a gallery wall" width="1558" height="1302" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Installation concept.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <ul class="points"><li>Coordinated leg motion and lighting create changing silhouettes.</li><li>Motion parameters include joint amplitude, phase offset, and transition duration.</li></ul>
    </section>

    <section id="control" class="space-y-5">
      <h2>Control Architecture</h2>
      <dl class="specs">
        <div><dt>Actuation</dt><dd>18 CyberGear motors</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Communication</dt><dd>2 CAN buses · 1 Mbit/s</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Host command rate</dt><dd>100 Hz</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <ul class="points">
        <li>Raspberry Pi runs the Python motion launcher and sends synchronized joint targets across both buses.</li>
        <li>Each motor receives position and velocity targets, PD gains, and torque feedforward; its internal controller closes the actuator loop.</li>
        <li>Session calibration maps joint coordinates to motor angles using offsets, signs, and gear ratios.</li>
      </ul>
      <HexapodArchitecture />
    </section>

    <section id="trajectory-generation" class="space-y-4">
      <h2>Trajectory Generation</h2>
      <figure>
        <img src="/media/hexapod/recognition-trajectories.png" alt="Planned recognition cue for legs 1 and 3: three panels overlay hip yaw, hip pitch, and knee offsets, with keyframes marked" width="1980" height="1440" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
      <ul class="points">
        <li>Joint-space keyframes specify hip yaw, hip pitch, and knee angles for each leg.</li>
        <li>Shape-preserving cubic interpolation carries velocity through intermediate poses and avoids keyframe overshoot.</li>
        <li>Phase offsets coordinate traveling waves; amplitude and time scaling adjust reach and speed.</li>
        <li>Hip-pitch peaks are 1.4 s apart. Staggered timing and different angular ranges give the gesture an organic rhythm.</li>
        <li>Validate calibrated travel and command limits; include startup alignment and a return trajectory.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="operator-interface" class="space-y-4">
      <h2>Operator Interface</h2>
      <figure id="dashboard">
        <img src="/media/hexapod/operator-preview.png" alt="TOCATL operator dashboard in preview mode, showing motion selection, amplitude, duration, and controller state" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>Operator dashboard in preview mode.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <ul class="points">
        <li>Initialize CAN and capture a session reference for the selected motors.</li>
        <li>Select a motion, adjust amplitude and duration, and preview the plan.</li>
        <li>Capture joint positions, record manual motion, and export run logs.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="safeguards" class="space-y-4">
      <h2>Execution Safeguards</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Software execution safeguards">
        <table><thead><tr><th>Check or control</th><th>Software behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><th>Session calibration</th><td>Require the selected motors’ reference offsets and calibrated limits before motion.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Trajectory limits</th><td>Validate plans before launch; distinguish soft-limit recovery from measured hard-boundary stops.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Feedback and faults</th><td>Monitor freshness and motor faults during execution; log recovery and stop events.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Cross-bus recovery</th><td>In the recorded test, a peer-bus failure triggered a 4.5-second return on the responding bus, followed by a latched hold.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Operator controls</th><td>Request a controlled return or immediate motor disable.</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="logging" class="space-y-4">
      <h2>Telemetry and Diagnostics</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Recorded signals">
        <table><thead><tr><th>Record</th><th>Signals</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><th>Motion feedback</th><td>Position, velocity, estimated torque, q-axis current</td><td>Tracking and actuator loading</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Motor health</th><td>Temperature, bus voltage, mode, faults</td><td>Thermal, supply, and fault diagnosis</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Feedback quality</th><td>Timestamp, motor/bus ID, freshness, data age</td><td>Identify delayed or missing replies</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Command and event logs</th><td>Targets, gains, execution phase, dispatch timing, CAN errors</td><td>Compare planned motion with execution</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
      </div>
      <figure id="recorded-telemetry">
        <a href="/media/hexapod/recognition-tracking.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open recorded position and feedback-age plot at full size">
          <img src="/media/hexapod/recognition-tracking.png" alt="Motor 2-2 command and measured position during a fault-triggered return, with feedback age for nine motors on can0" width="1800" height="1100" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <figcaption>August 24, 2026: motor 2-2 in motor coordinates; nine motors recorded on can0. A stale/missing-feedback report from can1 triggered the controlled return at 7.17 s.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="testing" class="space-y-4">
      <h2>Testing and Results</h2>
      <figure>
        <a href="/media/hexapod/command-pacing-before-after.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open measured command pacing before and after the fix at full size">
          <img src="/media/hexapod/command-pacing-before-after.png" alt="Recorded motor 3-1 host command intervals before and after the pacing fix: a 778 ms gap led to 39 rapid intervals of 0.73 to 1.52 ms; after a 780 ms gap, intervals remained about 18 to 20 ms. Separate 50 Hz tests, not CAN-wire timing." width="2240" height="896" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <figcaption>Motor 3-1, 50 Hz tests. Separate recordings of host command timing, not CAN-wire timing.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <ul class="points">
        <li><strong>Fault:</strong> recovery delays triggered catch-up bursts and transmit-buffer errors.</li>
        <li><strong>Change:</strong> reset overdue scheduling to resume at a paced cadence.</li>
        <li><strong>Retest:</strong> no transmit-buffer errors in the post-fix motion and recovery tests; intermittent feedback loss remained.</li>
      </ul>
      <div id="telemetry-plots" class="space-y-4 pt-4">
        <h2>Motion &amp; Motor Load</h2>
        <figure>
          <a href="/media/hexapod/motion-and-load.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open motor position and current plot at full size"><img src="/media/hexapod/motion-and-load.png" alt="Motor 2-2 commanded and measured position above its q-axis current, on a shared time axis during a 15-motor test" width="1800" height="1050" class="object-contain bg-white" loading="lazy" /></a>
          <figcaption>Motor 2-2 during a separate 15-motor test, August 24. Q-axis current indicates actuator effort, not battery current.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="walking-simulation" class="space-y-4">
      <h2>Walking Simulation</h2>
      <video autoplay loop controls muted playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/media/hexapod/simulation.png" class="w-full aspect-video object-contain"><source src="/media/hexapod/walk-simulation.mp4" type="video/mp4" /></video>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Walking-gait development in MuJoCo.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="closing" class="space-y-5" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
      <h2 id="closing-title">Closing</h2>
      <div class="closing-projects">
        <div>
          <h3>Autonomous Rover</h3>
          <video loop controls muted playsinline preload="metadata" aria-label="Autonomous rover project video">
            <source src="/media/autonomous-rover/hero.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
          <ul class="points"><li>Perception and behavior sequencing</li><li>Encoder-based wheel-speed control</li></ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Spider Hexapod</h3>
          <video loop controls muted playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/media/hexapod/spider-art-poster.jpg" aria-label="Spider hexapod art-motion video">
            <source src="/media/hexapod/spider-art.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
          <ul class="points"><li>Coordinated joint trajectories</li><li>Actuator communication and diagnostics</li></ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</ProjectLayout>

<style>
  [id] { scroll-margin-top: 7rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .points { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.3rem; color: var(--site-muted); line-height: 1.75; }
  .points li + li { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  figcaption { margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--site-muted); }
  .concept { max-width: 44rem; margin-inline: auto; }
  .overview-images { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .overview-images img { width: 100%; height: 320px; object-fit: contain; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .overview-images { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .overview-images img { height: auto; max-height: 320px; } }
  .specs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  .specs div { border-top: 2px solid var(--site-border); padding-top: 0.8rem; }
  dt { color: var(--site-muted); font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  dd { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6; text-align: left; }
  th, td { padding: 0.85rem 0.9rem; vertical-align: top; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--site-border); }
  thead th { background: var(--site-surface); }
  tbody th { font-weight: 500; width: 24%; }
  td { color: var(--site-muted); }
  @media (max-width: 640px) { .specs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } table { min-width: 590px; } }
</style>
